{% from "bits.njk" import contact %}

<section>
  <h2 id="information-we-collect">Information we may collect</h2>

  <h3>Account information</h3>
  <p>If you choose to create or connect an account, we may receive information necessary to authenticate you, such as your email address, account identifier, and basic profile information provided by authentication services such as Sign in with Apple or Sign in with Google.</p>
  <p>Apple or Google may limit the information they share with us according to your settings. For example, Apple may provide a private relay email address if you choose Hide My Email.</p>

  <h3>Recipe and cookbook information</h3>
  <p>FlavorDraft stores information you choose to save in your personal cookbook, which may include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>recipe titles</li>
    <li>ingredients</li>
    <li>preparation steps</li>
    <li>serving information</li>
    <li>notes</li>
    <li>collections</li>
    <li>favorites</li>
    <li>grocery-list information</li>
    <li>recipe source URLs</li>
    <li>source or creator attribution</li>
    <li>recipe images where applicable</li>
    <li>changes or adaptations you make to recipes</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="legal-note">
    <p>Your saved cookbook is private by default. FlavorDraft does not currently place your saved recipes into a central public recipe library for other users to browse.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Content you ask FlavorDraft to process</h3>
  <p>When you ask FlavorDraft to import or interpret a recipe, we may process information from the specific source you selected.</p>
  <p>Depending on the source, this may include publicly available:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>webpage text</li>
    <li>recipe metadata</li>
    <li>captions or descriptions</li>
    <li>audio or spoken information</li>
    <li>limited visual information needed to understand the recipe</li>
    <li>source links and attribution</li>
  </ul>
  <p>FlavorDraft processes this information to create or improve the private recipe notes you requested.</p>
  <p>FlavorDraft is designed around user-directed imports. We do not automatically add recipes from the internet to a public FlavorDraft recipe catalog.</p>

  <h3>AI interactions</h3>
  <p>If you use AI-assisted features, we may process the recipe context and the instructions or questions you provide.</p>
  <p>For example, you might ask FlavorDraft to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>make vague cooking steps clearer</li>
    <li>adjust serving quantities</li>
    <li>suggest substitutions</li>
    <li>reorganize recipe instructions</li>
    <li>adapt a recipe for a preference</li>
    <li>turn a dish idea into a recipe</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Information needed to respond may be sent to third-party AI service providers acting as service providers to FlavorDraft.</p>

  <h3>Device and technical information</h3>
  <p>We may receive limited technical information needed to operate, secure, diagnose, and improve the Service, such as:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>device and operating-system information</li>
    <li>app version</li>
    <li>network or request information</li>
    <li>crash or diagnostic information</li>
    <li>security and abuse-prevention information</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="how-we-use-information">How we use information</h2>
  <p>We may use information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>provide and maintain FlavorDraft</li>
    <li>authenticate users</li>
    <li>save and synchronize a user’s cookbook</li>
    <li>process user-requested recipe imports</li>
    <li>generate structured recipe notes</li>
    <li>provide AI-assisted recipe features</li>
    <li>create grocery lists and other user-requested features</li>
    <li>maintain source attribution and source links</li>
    <li>diagnose errors and improve reliability</li>
    <li>prevent abuse and protect the security of the Service</li>
    <li>provide customer support</li>
    <li>comply with applicable legal obligations</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal information. FlavorDraft is not designed around advertising.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="private-cookbooks">Private cookbooks</h2>
  <p>Recipes and collections saved in FlavorDraft are intended to function as a user’s personal cookbook. They are private by default.</p>
  <p>FlavorDraft does not currently operate a public community recipe feed or automatically publish users’ saved recipes for other FlavorDraft users to discover.</p>
  <p>If sharing or public publishing features are introduced in the future, users should be given clear controls before their private content becomes public, and this Privacy Policy should be updated accordingly.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="user-directed-processing">User-directed recipe processing</h2>
  <p>FlavorDraft helps automate actions a user could otherwise perform manually when taking recipe notes.</p>
  <p>A user selects a recipe, webpage, video, social post, or other supported source and asks FlavorDraft to process it. FlavorDraft may then analyze relevant information from that source to create structured notes for that user’s private cookbook.</p>
  <p>Where available and appropriate, FlavorDraft attempts to preserve information identifying the original source or creator and a link back to the source.</p>
  <p>FlavorDraft does not claim ownership of third-party source content.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="service-providers">Service providers</h2>
  <p>We may use third-party service providers to operate FlavorDraft. These may include providers for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>cloud infrastructure and database services</li>
    <li>authentication</li>
    <li>AI and machine-learning processing</li>
    <li>security and abuse prevention</li>
    <li>diagnostics and operational reliability</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For example, FlavorDraft currently uses Supabase for parts of its backend infrastructure and authentication system, and may use AI technology provided by companies such as OpenAI and Google for certain recipe-processing or assistance features.</p>
  <p>These providers may process limited information on our behalf when necessary to provide their services. Their handling of information is also governed by their own terms and privacy practices.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="data-retention">Data retention</h2>
  <p>We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary to provide the Service, maintain your account and cookbook, comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes, enforce agreements, and protect FlavorDraft and its users. The exact retention period may depend on the type of information and why it is being processed.</p>
  <p>When you delete information from FlavorDraft, some copies may remain temporarily in backups, logs, or systems where immediate deletion is not technically practical, or where retention is required for legitimate legal or security purposes.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="data-security">Data security</h2>
  <p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures intended to protect information handled by FlavorDraft. However, no internet-connected service or storage system can guarantee absolute security.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="your-choices">Your choices</h2>
  <p>Depending on the features available in the app, you may be able to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>edit or delete recipes</li>
    <li>remove recipes from collections</li>
    <li>change account or profile information</li>
    <li>sign out</li>
    <li>request deletion of your account and associated personal information</li>
    <li>control permissions through iOS settings</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To make a request about your information, contact {{ contact(site) }}.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="childrens-privacy">Children’s privacy</h2>
  <p>FlavorDraft is not directed to children under the minimum age required to independently consent to use online services in their jurisdiction. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children in violation of applicable law.</p>
  <p>If you believe a child has provided personal information improperly, contact us.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="international-users">International users</h2>
  <p>FlavorDraft and its service providers may process information in countries other than the country in which you live. Where required by applicable law, we take appropriate steps relating to international transfers of personal information.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy as FlavorDraft evolves. If we make material changes, we will update the effective date and, where appropriate, provide additional notice.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>For questions about this Privacy Policy or privacy requests, contact:</p>
  <p>{{ contact(site) }}</p>
</section>
